{
  "amendment_reason": "Non-termination is now bounded by iterations rather than detected by timeout, so the measurement no longer depends on machine load. Prior: E70b was contaminated by false timeouts, detected by the null_only control scoring -0.4444 where exactly 0.0 is required by construction. Timeout is now calibrated from measured runtime and the champion is measured best-of-three. Prior context: E70's plan was not executable: a 15s candidate timeout against a 25-58% non-termination rate made the run take >20h. Killed after 2h11m with zero output and no report file, so no result informed this amendment. Timeout 15s -> 0.5s, budget 200 -> 150, seeds 5 -> 3.",
  "amends": "E70c-governed-search",
  "budget_per_arm": 150,
  "capability_claim_boundary": "Any positive result is a claim about a generic mutation search on four small Python tasks. It is NOT evidence of model self-improvement, of a recursive effect, or of anything about the scaffold improving itself. The proposer is an AST mutator with no model in the loop.",
